lines+=['','Differences are the shortest separation between axes, from 0 to 90 degrees, allowing for 180 degree equivalence. No galaxy-specific correction was chosen to minimise a difference. Each hypothesis applies the same rule to every galaxy.','', 'The 51 screened objects were selected without using agreement with Euclid: a completed unflagged fit, complete cutout, inclination 40 to 70 degrees, disc PA radial scatter below 3 degrees, bar upper interval bound above 2 arcsec, and fitted sky PA within 15 degrees of north–south or east–west. This last requirement makes a sign reversal distinguishable from a quarter turn. With the 90 degree adjustment, 48 of 51 agree within 10 degrees; with reversed sign, none do.','', 'Across all 546 unflagged fits, 433 agree within 10 degrees after the adjustment, compared with 71 for reversed sign and 2 for the current conversion. Photutils is not ground truth: whole-object catalogue shapes and selected outer-disc ellipses can legitimately differ.','', '## Six visual examples','', 'Three examples in each cardinal-axis group were selected by largest bar upper interval bound, rather than by Euclid agreement. All six images were inspected. Orange ellipses use Euclid shape parameters at three times the catalogue size, solely to make the orientation visible. Cyan ellipses are reliable points in the selected Photutils disc range. Native images are displayed without rotation or reflection.','', '| Galaxy ID | Photutils disc PA | Experimental adjusted sky PA | Difference after adjustment | Difference with sign reversal |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
