lines+=['## What has been saved','', '`MER_VIS_experimental_PA_manifest.csv` retains all 2777 target rows and all original columns and values. New experimental columns include:','', '- `experimental_current_sky_pa_deg`: independent conversion using two positions in the native cutout WCS.','- `experimental_plus90_sky_pa_deg`: input pixel angle plus 90 degrees, independently transformed through WCS.','- `experimental_reverse_sign_sky_pa_deg`: negated input angle, independently transformed through WCS.','- `experimental_raw_as_sky_sky_pa_deg`: raw catalogue angle treated as an already defined sky PA, diagnostic only.','- `experimental_stored_sky_plus90_deg`: exactly `(euclid_detection_pa_sky_deg + 90) % 180`, the proposed simple adjustment to the existing converted column.','- Corresponding absolute differences from Photutils, plus hypothesis calculation status.','', 'The pixel-plus-90 and sky-plus-90 methods are effectively equivalent for these locally square, orthogonal pixel grids. Their endpoint estimates can differ slightly because a finite 10-pixel direction on a spherical projection is used for the independent check. The maximum difference between the independent current conversion and the original stored conversion across all targets is 0.000000156 degrees.','', 'Failed Photutils fits remain failed. Experimental catalogue directions may still be calculated for them, but their differences from unavailable fitted geometry are blank. No missing angle is replaced by zero.','', '## Interpretation and recommended use','', 'The test rejects a simple input sign reversal as the explanation for the systematic mismatch in this sample. The quarter turn gives both much better numerical agreement and visibly plausible ellipse directions across multiple orientations. It is therefore reasonable to use the separately labelled adjusted column for exploratory comparisons, with the empirical convention adjustment explicitly recorded.','', 'The original detection mosaic is not publicly distributed in Q1. We have not established why the catalogue values require this treatment relative to the released science mosaic WCS. The raw-as-sky hypothesis also performs similarly to the quarter-turn hypothesis on these nearly north-up mosaics; these data do not identify the precise pipeline convention. Do not claim that this proves a universal conversion for other releases or image frames, or that it independently validates every physical disc orientation.','', 'The original fitting manifest SHA256 before and after this experiment is '+s['original_manifest_sha256']+'. The source file was not modified. No production deprojection settings or original Euclid catalogue values have been overwritten.','', 'Reproducible code: `Euclid/validation_MER_VIS/compare_MER_VIS_PA_hypotheses.py`. The original full-mosaic validation and its download integrity caveat remain documented one folder above.']
